//
// PROBE: words that were implemented and run by no golden.
//
// `cargo xtask coverage` listed nineteen. These eight can be held by a golden;
// the other eleven cannot, and F175 says why for each.
//
// Where an answer depends on chance the word runs and its value is dropped,
// as `coverage-host.bund` does: the closing stack dump still pins that it ran
// without error and left what its effect says.

"probe: ?key leaves the container and pushes whether the key is there" println
dict "a" 1 set "a" ?key println drop
dict "a" 1 set "b" ?key println drop

"probe: ?ifthenelse builds a conditional whose :if slot decides between the other two" println
?ifthenelse
  :if { true } set
  :then { "then ran" println } set
  :else { "else ran" println } set
!
?ifthenelse
  :if { false } set
  :then { "then ran" println } set
  :else { "else ran" println } set
!

"probe: ls is fs.ls, counted over a fixed tree" println
"tests/probes/data/ls" ls len println drop

"probe: rm is fs.rm" println
[ "/tmp/bund2-probe-gap.txt" ] rm drop
"x" "/tmp/bund2-probe-gap.txt" file.write
"/tmp/bund2-probe-gap.txt" fs.is_file println
[ "/tmp/bund2-probe-gap.txt" ] rm drop
"/tmp/bund2-probe-gap.txt" fs.is_file println

"probe: the stemming tokenizer answers a set, so only its size is fixed" println
"The runners were running quickly" string.tokenize.stemmed len println drop
"The runners were running quickly" . string.tokenize.stemmed. len println drop

"probe: words whose answer is chance run, and are dropped" println
math.securerandom.int drop
string.random.name drop
"done" println
